# Anti Double Reserve Concern

## Scope
Prevent duplicate stock reservation for same product using distributed locks per reservation token - only one operation per reservation token at a time.

## Out of Scope
Lock hierarchies, lock escalation, deadlock detection beyond simple TTL, multi-token coordination.

# Aftermath target
After completion: distributed lock acquisition per reservation token, lock release on completion, concurrent requests rejected with clear error. No product reserved twice for same reservation token.

## Definition of Done
[ ] Lock acquisition: acquire lock per reservation token
    [ ] Verification: `console.log('TRACE: Lock acquisition attempted', { token, operation })` on request start
    [ ] Verification: `console.log('TRACE: Lock acquired', { token, ttl })` when lock successful
    [ ] Test: Acquire lock, verify lock held in Redis
[ ] Lock rejection: reject concurrent requests
    [ ] Verification: `console.log('TRACE: Lock rejected', { token, reason: 'already_held' })` on concurrent request
    [ ] Test: Send 3 requests with same token simultaneously, verify only 1 processed, 2 rejected
[ ] Lock release: release lock on completion
    [ ] Verification: `console.log('TRACE: Lock released', { token })` on operation completion
    [ ] Test: Complete operation, verify lock removed from Redis
